.TH "STYLEPROPERTYMAP.SET" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
StylePropertyMap.set \- StylePropertyMap: set() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]set()\f[B]\f[R] method of the \f[CR]StylePropertyMap\f[R]
interface changes the CSS declaration using the given property.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
set(property)
set(property, value1)
set(property, value1, value2)
set(property, value1, value2, /* \&..., */ valueN)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]property\f[R]
An identifier indicating the stylistic feature (e.g., font, width,
background color) to change.
.TP
\f[B]value1\f[R], \&..., \f[B]valueN\f[R]
The value(s) the given property should have.
.SS Return value
None (\f[CR]undefined\f[R]).
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
This example sets the specified value for the \f[CR]padding\-top\f[R]
property within the element\(cqs style attribute.
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// get the button element\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] buttonEl = document.querySelector(\(dqbutton\(dq);

\f[I]// set padding\-top on button style attribute\f[R]
buttonEl.attributeStyleMap.set(\(dqpadding\-top\(dq, CSS.px(10));
.EE
